===Proper noun===
{{en-prop|ies|s}}

# {{senseid|en|Q108}}The first [[month]] of the [[Gregorian calendar]], following the [[December]] of the previous year and preceding [[February]]. Abbreviation: '''[[Jan]]''' or '''[[Jan.]]'''
#: ''01/01/09'' : [[Thursday]], 1st '''January'''(,) 2009.
#: ''American style:'' [[Thursday]], '''January''' 1st, 2009.
#: {{ux|en|I hate '''January'''s: it's always too cold.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Amir Vera|title=Louisville detective who fatally shot Breonna Taylor is appealing his termination from the police department|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/12/13/us/myles-cosgrove-breonna-taylor-termination-appeal-hearing/index.html|date=2021-12-13|passage=The Louisville Metro Police Department terminated Detective Myles Cosgrove in '''January''' for use of deadly force for firing 16 rounds into Taylor’s home and failing to activate his body camera, according to a copy of his termination letter.}}
# {{lb|en|rare}} {{given name|en|female|from=month names < English}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Michael Schofield|title=January First
|passage=“Hi, '''January'''!” Lynn calls. “Happy birthday!”}}

